            "english": "God then said, \"Let there be sources of light in the sky to separate day from night. Let them serve as markers for holy days, seasons, days, and years."
            "english": "and to shine in the day and the night, and to separate the light from the darkness. God saw that this was good."
            "english": "God also said, \"Let the waters be filled with every type of living creature, and let birds fly above the earth, across the sky.\""
            "english": "So God created the great sea monsters and every other living creature that moves, which filled the waters, each according to its species. He also created every winged bird according to its species. God saw that this was good."
            "english": "God said, \"Let the earth bring forth animals according to their kinds: cattle, creatures that move along the ground, and wild animals, each according to its species.\" And so it was."
            "english": "So God created man in His own image, giving them reason and free will; in the image of God, He created him. He created male and female."
            "english": "Then God said, \"Look, I have given you every seed-bearing plant on the face of the entire earth, and every tree whose fruit contains seeds. These will be your food."
            "english": "So the Lord God formed man from the dust of the ground, and He breathed into his face the breath of life, and man received a living soul."
            "english": "Then the Lord God had planted the Garden of Paradise in the beginning towards the East, and there He placed the man whom He had formed."
            "english": "A river flowed out of the place of delight to water the Garden, and from there it divided into four branches."
            "english": "Therefore, the Lord God took the man and placed him in the Garden of Paradise to cultivate and keep it."
            "english": "And the Lord God gave the man this command, saying: \"From every tree of the Garden you may freely eat."
            "english": "Now, the serpent was the most cunning creature among all the animals the Lord God had made on the earth. It came to the woman and said, 'Why did God give you a command that you should not eat from *any* tree in this entire Garden?' —the serpent twisted God's actual prohibition, making it sound like they were forbidden from everything."
            "english": "The woman answered the serpent, 'We may eat the fruit from the trees throughout the Garden;'"
            "english": "but from the fruit of the tree that stands in the very center of the Garden, God has strictly commanded us not to eat, nor even to touch it—an addition the woman made to God's original command—lest we die.'"
            "english": "And when they heard the voice of the Lord God, Who was walking about in the Garden during the cool afternoon breeze, Adam and his wife immediately hid themselves from the presence of the Lord God, concealing themselves among the trees of the garden."
            "english": "He answered, 'I heard Your voice in the Garden, and I was afraid because I was naked, so I hid myself.'"
            "english": "And Adam said, 'The woman that You gave to be my companion—she gave me fruit from the tree, and I ate it.'"
            "english": "I will put conflict, a spiritual warfare, between you and the woman, and between your offspring and her offspring. She, the Woman, shall crush your head—a prophecy of Mary and her Son, Jesus Christ, triumphing over you—and you, in turn, shall lie in wait for her heel, attempting to wound Him."
            "english": "To the woman He also said, 'I will greatly multiply your sorrows and your painful. In great pain you shall give birth to children. You shall be subject to your husband's authority, and he shall rule over you.'"
            "english": "With the sweat of your face and much labor you shall have food to eat, and this shall be so until you return to the very ground from which you were taken; for you are dust, and to dust you shall return in death."
            "english": "And the Lord God said, 'Behold, Adam has now become like one of Us— knowing good and evil, yet in a corrupt way. Now, I shall stop him, so that he may not reach out his hand and also take from the Tree of Life, and eat, and live forever in this fallen state—'"
            "english": "Therefore, the Lord God sent Adam out from the Garden of Eden—the Garden of Paradise—so that he might work the very ground from which he was taken, as a consequence of his sin."
            "english": "And so He drove Adam out; and at the eastern side of the Garden of Paradise, He stationed Cherubim and a flaming sword that turned every way, to guard the path to the Tree of Life and prevent humanity from reaching it in their fallen state."
            "english": "Again, she gave birth to his brother, Abel. Abel became a shepherd of sheep, while Cain was a farmer of the ground."
            "english": "Abel also offered from the firstborn of his flock and from their best portions. The Lord looked with favor upon Abel and his offering, for he gave the best of what he had."
            "english": "But the Lord God did not approve of Cain and his offering. Cain became extremely angry, and he became sorrowful."
            "english": "Then the Lord said to Cain, \"Why are you angry? Why is your face full of sorrow?\""
            "english": "If you do what is right, will you be accepted. But if you do not do what is right, sin is waiting at the door, and its desire is for you, but you must master it."
            "english": "Then the Lord said to Cain, \"Where is your brother Abel?\" He answered, \"I do not know. Am I my brother's guardian?\""
            "english": "And He said to him, \"What have you done? The voice of your brother's blood is crying out to me from the earth!\"- for the murder of the innocent cries out for vengeance to God"
            "english": "Now, therefore, you are cursed while you live upon the earth, which has opened its mouth to receive your brother's blood, shed by your hand."
            "english": "When you cultivate the ground, it will no longer give its produce to you. You shall be a restless wanderer on the earth."
            "english": "To Enoch was born Irad. Irad was the father of Maviael. Maviael was the father of Mathusael, and Mathusael was the father of Lamech."
            "english": "He created one male and one female. He blessed them, and He called their collective name 'Mankind' (Adam), at the time they were created."
            "english": "Adam lived for one hundred and thirty years, and then he became the father of a son in his own image and likeness, whom he named Seth."
            "english": "After he begot Seth, Adam lived for eight hundred more years, during which time he also had other sons and daughters."
            "english": "Seth also lived for one hundred and five years, and then he had a son named Enos."
