            "english": "After he had his child Enoch, Jared lived for eight hundred more years, during which time he also had other sons and daughters."
            "english": "Enoch lived for sixty-five years, and then he had a son named Methuselah."
            "english": "And Enoch walked closely with God, remaining in God's favor. After he had a son named Methuselah, Enoch lived for three hundred more years, during which time he also had other sons and daughters."
            "english": "Methuselah also lived for one hundred and eighty-seven years, and then he had a son named Lamech."
            "english": "After he had his child Lamech, Methuselah lived for seven hundred and eighty-two more years, during which time he also had other sons and daughters."
            "english": "Lamech lived for one hundred and eighty-two years, and then he had a son."
            "latin": "Noe vero cum quingentorum esset annorum, genuit Sem, Cham, et Japheth.",
            "english": "the sons of God, who were the descendants of Seth, saw that the daughters of men were beautiful, and they chose wives for themselves from all of them whom they desired."
            "english": "God said, \"I will cleanse man whom I have created from the face of the earth—from man to beast, from creeping thing to the birds of the sky—for I regret that I have made them : for the great sins of man brought God's judgment upon the world.\""
            "english": "And Noah had three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth."
            "english": "The earth's people, however, were corrupt and sinned against God; the earth was filled with their sin and violence."
            "english": "When God saw that the earth's inhabitants were corrupted (for all of mankind had corrupted its way upon the earth—their moral path was depraved),"
            "english": "God said to Noah, \"The end of all mankind has come; for the earth is filled with sin and violence because of them. And behold, I will destroy them with the earth.\""
            "english": "And this is how you shall make it: The length of the ark shall be three hundred cubits, its width fifty cubits, and its height thirty cubits. (A cubit is approximately 18 inches, the Ark was about 450 feet long, 75 feet wide, 45 feet high)."
            "english": "For behold, I am bringing a flood upon the earth, to destroy all mankind. Everything that is on the earth shall die."
            "english": "And from every living thing, you shall bring two of every sort into the ark, to keep them alive with you; of the two one shall be male and the other one female."
            "english": "Of the birds, livestock, and every creeping thing of the earth, two of each shall come to you, so they may live."
            "english": "Thus Noah did all that God had commanded him to do."
            "english": "\"And from the birds of the sky, take seven pairs of each, a male and a female. This is so that their offspring may be preserved on the earth after the flood.\""
            "english": "\"For in exactly seven days, I will send rain upon the earth for forty days and forty nights. I will then wipe out every living thing that I have made from the surface of the earth.\""
            "english": "All the animals, both clean and unclean, and all the birds, and all the creeping creatures that move upon the earth—a sign signifying the Catholic Church, in which both all peoples must enter to be saved."
            "english": "God wiped out every living thing that was on the surface of the earth, from man to domestic animal, and all creeping creatures, and all birds of the sky. They were all utterly destroyed from the earth. Only Noah remained alive, along with those who were with him in the ark, this signifies that there is no salvation outside ofthe Catholic Church which is of the ark of salvation. "
            "english": "And all the living creatures, all the creeping things, and all the birds, everything that moves upon the earth, came out of the ark."
            "english": "Then Noah built an altar to the Lord. And taking from every clean animal and every clean bird, he offered sacrifice by burning offerings on the altar."
            "english": "And the Lord smelled the pleasing aroma of the sacrifice, and He said in His heart: 'Never again will I curse the earth because of humans, for the intention and the inclination of the human heart are prone to evil even from its youth, because of Original Sin. Therefore, I will never again strike down every living thing as I have done."
            "english": "Every living thing that moves will be food for you. Just as I gave you the green plants before the flood, I have now given you all these things to eat."
            "english": "For I will certainly execute justice upon for those who shed your blood; I will execute it upon every wild beast and man. Indeed, upon every man and his brother, I will execute justice upon those who take the life of a human being."
            "english": "Whoever sheds human blood, his blood shall also be shed in return; for indeed, God made man in His own divine image and likeness, for the murder of the innocent cries to heaven for vengeance."
            "english": "\"I establish my covenant with you: never again shall all living creatures be cut be destroyed by the waters of a flood; nor shall there ever again be a flood to destroy the entire earth.\""
            "english": "He said, \"Cursed by God is Canaan! He shall be the lowest of servants to his brothers.\""
            "english": "These are the descendants of Noah's sons, Shem, Ham, and Japheth. Children were born to the three sons of Noah after the great flood that cleansed the earth of humanity."
            "english": "These are the family groups which descended from Noah, according to their peoples and nations. From these, the nations of the earth spread out and divided after the great flood."
            "english": "But then the Lord's judgment came down from His sublime dwelling to judge the city and the tower that the children of Adam were building."
            "english": "Then He said, 'Come, let Us —Father, Son and Holy Spirit: the Holy Trinity— bring down our judgment upon them and confuse their language, so that no one will be able to understand what his neighbor is saying.'"
