          {
            "number": 34,
            "latin": "Concepitque tertio, et genuit alium filium : dixitque : Nunc quoque copulabitur mihi maritus meus : eo quod pepererim ei tres filios : et idcirco appellavit nomen ejus Levi.",
            "english": "And she conceived the third time, and bore another son: and said: Now also my husband will be joined to me, because I have borne him three sons: and therefore she called his name Levi."
          },
          {
            "number": 35,
            "latin": "Quarto concepit, et peperit filium, et ait : Modo confitebor Domino, et ob hoc vocavit eum Judam : cessavitque parere.",
            "english": "The fourth time she conceived and bore a son, and said: now will I praise the Lord: and for this she called him Juda. And she left bearing."
          },
          {
            "number": 41,
            "latin": "Igitur quando primo tempore ascendebantur oves, ponebat Jacob virgas in canalibus aquarum ante oculos arietum et ovium, ut in earum contemplatione conciperent :",
            "english": "So when the ewes went first to ram, Jacob put the rods in the troughs of water before the eyes of the rams, and of the ewes, that they might conceive while they were looking upon them:"
          },
          {
            "number": 42,
            "latin": "quando vero serotina admissura erat, et conceptus extremus, non ponebat eas. Factaque sunt ea quae erant serotina, Laban : et quae primi temporis, Jacob.",
            "english": "But when the latter coming was, and the last conceiving, he did not put them. And those that were lateward, became Laban's: and they of the first time, Jacob's."
          },
          {
            "number": 43,
            "latin": "Ditatusque est homo ultra modum, et habuit greges multos, ancillas et servos, camelos et asinos.",
            "english": "And the man was enriched exceedingly, and he had many flocks, maid servants and men servants, camels and asses."
            "number": 35,
            "latin": "ait: Ne irascatur dominus meus, quod surgere coram te non valeo, quia mos feminarum mihi accidit. Ita fefellit patrem, nec invenit quod quærebat.",
            "english": "she said, \"Do not be angry, my lord, that I cannot rise in your presence, for I am experiencing a woman's customary condition.\" In this way, she deceived her father, and he did not find what he was looking for."
          },
          {
            "number": 36,
            "latin": "Iratus est igitur Jacob, et jurgatus est cum Laban: et ait: Quid est delictum meum, et peccatum, cur me sic insecutus es?",
            "english": "Then Jacob became angry and argued with Laban. He said, \"What is my offense? What is my sin that you have pursued me so fiercely?\""
          },
          {
            "number": 37,
            "latin": "Perquisitis omnibus supellectilibus meis, quid ex rebus domus tuae invenisti? Pone hic coram fratribus meis et fratribus tuis, et judicent inter utrumque nostrum.",
            "english": "\"After you have thoroughly searched through all my possessions, what have you found here that belongs to your household? Place it here before my kinsmen and your kinsmen, and let them judge between us.\""
          },
          {
            "number": 38,
            "latin": "Viginti annis fui tecum: oves tuae et caprae steriles non fuerunt, arietes gregis tui non comedi.",
            "english": "\"I have been with you for twenty years. Your ewes and female goats were never barren, and I never ate the rams from your flock.\""
          },
          {
            "number": 39,
            "latin": "Nec raptum a bestia ostendi tibi, omnem damni sarcinam ego sustinui: quidquid furto perierat, a me exigebas.",
            "english": "\"I never showed you an animal torn by wild beasts; I always bore the burden of such loss myself. Whatever was stolen, you demanded compensation from me.\""
          },
          {
            "number": 40,
            "latin": "Die noctuque aestu torquebar, et gelu, et fugiebat somnus ab oculis meis.",
            "english": "\"By day, I was tormented by the scorching heat, and by night, by the bitter frost. Sleep often fled from my eyes.\""
          },
          {
            "number": 41,
            "latin": "Sicque per viginti annos in domo tua servivi tibi, quatuordecim pro filiabus, et sex pro gregibus tuis : immutasti quoque mercedem meam decem vicibus.",
            "english": "And in this manner have I served you in your house twenty years, fourteen for your daughters, and six for your flocks: you have changed also my wages ten times."
          },
          {
            "number": 42,
            "latin": "Nisi Deus patris mei Abraham, et timor Isaac affuisset mihi, forsitan modo nudum me demisisses : afflictionem meam et laborem manuum mearum respexit Deus, et arguit te heri.",
            "english": "Unless the God of my father Abraham, and the fear of Isaac had stood by me, peradventure now you hadst sent me away naked: God beheld my affliction and the labour of my hands, and rebuked you yesterday."
          },
          {
            "number": 43,
            "latin": "Respondit ei Laban : Filiae meae et filii, et greges tui, et omnia quae cernis, mea sunt : quid possum facere filiis et nepotibus meis?",
            "english": "Laban answered him: The daughters are mine and the children, and your flocks, and all things that you seest are mine: what can I do to my children, and grandchildren?"
          },
          {
            "number": 44,
            "latin": "Veni ergo, et ineamus foedus, ut sit in testimonium inter me et te.",
            "english": "Come therefore, let us enter into a league: that it may be for a testimony between me and you."
          },
          {
            "number": 45,
            "latin": "Tulit itaque Jacob lapidem, et erexit illum in titulum :",
            "english": "And Jacob took a stone, and set it up for a title:"
          },
          {
            "number": 46,
            "latin": "dixitque fratribus suis : Afferte lapides. Qui congregantes fecerunt tumulum, comederuntque super eum :",
            "english": "And he said to his brethren: Bring hither stones. And they gathering stones together, made a heap, and they ate upon it."
          },
          {
            "number": 47,
            "latin": "quem vocavit Laban Tumulum testis : et Jacob, Acervum testimonii, uterque juxta proprietatem linguae suae.",
            "english": "And Laban called it The witness heap: and Jacob, The hillock of testimony: each of them according to the propriety of his language."
          },
          {
            "number": 48,
            "latin": "Dixitque Laban : Tumulus iste erit testis inter me et te hodie, et idcirco appellatum est nomen ejus Galaad, id est, Tumulus testis.",
            "english": "And Laban said: This heap shall be a witness between me and you this day, and therefore the name of it was called Galaad, that is, The witness heap."
          },
          {
            "number": 49,
            "latin": "Intueatur et judicet Dominus inter nos quando recesserimus a nobis,",
            "english": "The Lord look and judge between us when we shall be gone one from the other."
            "number": 50,
            "latin": "si afflixeris filias meas, et si introduxeris alias uxores super eas : nullus sermonis nostri testis est absque Deo, qui praesens respicit.",
            "english": "If you afflict my daughters, and if you bring in other wives over them: none is witness of our speech but God, who is present and beholdeth."
            "number": 51,
            "latin": "Dixitque rursus ad Jacob : En tumulus hic, et lapis quem erexi inter me et te,",
            "english": "And he said again to Jacob: Look, this heap, and the stone which I have set up between me and you,"
            "number": 52,
            "latin": "testis erit : tumulus, inquam, iste et lapis sint in testimonium, si aut ego transiero illum pergens ad te, aut tu praeterieris, malum mihi cogitans.",
            "english": "Shall be a witness: this heap, I say, and the stone, be they for a testimony, if either I shall pass beyond it going towards you, or you shall pass beyond it, thinking harm to me."
            "number": 53,
            "latin": "Deus Abraham, et Deus Nachor, judicet inter nos, Deus patris eorum. Juravit ergo Jacob per timorem patris sui Isaac :",
            "english": "The God of Abraham, and the God of Nachor, the God of their father, judge between us. And Jacob swore by the fear of his father Isaac."
            "number": 54,
            "latin": "immolatisque victimis in monte, vocavit fratres suos ut ederent panem. Qui cum comedissent, manserunt ibi :",
            "english": "And after he had offered sacrifices in the mountain, he called his brethren to eat bread. And when they had eaten, they lodged there:"
          },
          {
            "number": 55,
            "latin": "Laban vero de nocte consurgens, osculatus est filios, et filias suas, et benedixit illis : reversusque est in locum suum.",
            "english": "But Laban arose in the night, and kissed his sons, and daughters, and blessed them: and returned to his place."
          },
          {
            "number": 41,
            "latin": "dux Oolibama, dux Ela, dux Phinon,",
            "english": "Duke Oolibama, duke Ela, duke Phinon,"
          },
          {
            "number": 42,
            "latin": "dux Cenez, dux Theman, dux Mabsar,",
            "english": "Duke Cenez, duke Theman, duke Mabsar,"
          },
          {
            "number": 43,
            "latin": "dux Magdiel, dux Hiram : hi duces Edom habitantes in terra imperii sui, ipse est Esau pater Idumaeorum.",
            "english": "Duke Magdiel, duke Hiram: these are the dukes of Edom dwelling in the land of their government; the same is Esau the father of the Edomites."
          },
          {
            "number": 41,
            "latin": "Dixitque rursus Pharao ad Joseph : Ecce, constitui te super universam terram Aegypti.",
            "english": "And again Pharao said to Joseph: Look, I have appointed you over the whole land of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 42,
            "latin": "Tulitque annulum de manu sua, et dedit eum in manu ejus : vestivitque eum stola byssina, et collo torquem auream circumposuit.",
            "english": "And he took his ring from his own hand, and gave it into his hand: and he put upon him a robe of silk, and put a chain of gold about his neck."
          },
          {
            "number": 43,
            "latin": "Fecitque eum ascendere super currum suum secundum, clamante praecone, ut omnes coram eo genu flecterent, et praepositum esse scirent universae terrae Aegypti.",
            "english": "And he made him go up into his second chariot, the crier proclaiming that all should bow their knee before him, and that they should know he was made governor over the whole land of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 44,
            "latin": "Dixit quoque rex ad Joseph : Ego sum Pharao : absque tuo imperio non movebit quisquam manum aut pedem in omni terra Aegypti.",
            "english": "And the king said to Joseph: I am Pharao; without your commandment no man shall move hand or foot in all the land of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 45,
            "latin": "Vertitque nomen ejus, et vocavit eum, lingua aegyptiaca, Salvatorem mundi. Deditque illi uxorem Aseneth filiam Putiphare sacerdotis Heliopoleos. Egressus est itaque Joseph ad terram Aegypti",
            "english": "And he turned his name, and called him in the Egyptian tongue, The saviour of the world. And he gave him to wife Aseneth the daughter of Putiphare priest of Heliopolis. Then Joseph went out to the land of Egypt:"
          },
          {
            "number": 46,
            "latin": "( triginta autem annorum erat quando stetit in conspectu regis Pharaonis), et circuivit omnes regiones Aegypti.",
            "english": "(Now he was thirty years old when he stood before king Pharao) and he went round all the countries of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 47,
            "latin": "Venitque fertilitas septem annorum : et in manipulos redactae segetes congregatae sunt in horrea Aegypti.",
            "english": "And the fruitfulness of the seven years came: and the corn being bound up into sheaves was gathered together into the barns of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 48,
            "latin": "Omnis etiam frugum abundantia in singulis urbibus condita est.",
            "english": "And all the abundance of grain was laid up in every city."
          },
          {
            "number": 49,
            "latin": "Tantaque fuit abundantia tritici, ut arenae maris coaequaretur, et copia mensuram excederet.",
            "english": "And there was so great abundance of wheat, that it was equal to the sand of the sea, and the plenty exceeded measure."
          },
          {
            "number": 50,
            "latin": "Nati sunt autem Joseph filii duo antequam veniret fames : quos peperit ei Aseneth filia Putiphare sacerdotis Heliopoleos.",
            "english": "And before the famine came, Joseph had two sons born: whom Aseneth the daughter of Putiphare priest of Heliopolis bore to him."
          },
          {
            "number": 51,
            "latin": "Vocavitque nomen primogeniti Manasses, dicens : Oblivisci me fecit Deus omnium laborum meorum, et domus patris mei.",
            "english": "And he called the name of the firstborn Manasses, saying: God has made me to forget all my labours, and my father's house."
          },
          {
            "number": 52,
            "latin": "Nomen quoque secundi appellavit Ephraim, dicens : Crescere me fecit Deus in terra paupertatis meae.",
            "english": "And he named the second Ephraim, saying: God has made me to grow in the land of my poverty."
          },
          {
            "number": 53,
            "latin": "Igitur transactis septem ubertatis annis, qui fuerant in Aegypto,",
            "english": "Now when the seven years of the plenty that had been in Egypt were past:"
          },
          {
            "number": 54,
            "latin": "coeperunt venire septem anni inopiae, quos praedixerat Joseph : et in universo orbe fames praevaluit, in cuncta autem terra Aegypti panis erat.",
            "english": "The seven years of scarcity, which Joseph had foretold, began to come: and the famine prevailed in the whole world, but there was bread in all the land of Egypt."
          },
          {
            "number": 55,
            "latin": "Qua esuriente, clamavit populus ad Pharaonem, alimenta petens. Quibus ille respondit : Ite ad Joseph : et quidquid ipse vobis dixerit, facite.",
            "english": "And when there also they began to be famished, the people cried to Pharao for food. And he said to them: Go to Joseph: and do all that he shall say to you."
          },
          {
            "number": 56,
            "latin": "Crescebat autem quotidie fames in omni terra : aperuitque Joseph universa horrea, et vendebat Aegyptiis : nam et illos oppresserat fames.",
            "english": "And the famine increased daily in all the land: and Joseph opened all the barns, and sold to the Egyptians: for the famine had oppressed them also."
          },
          {
            "number": 57,
            "latin": "Omnesque provinciae veniebant in Aegyptum, ut emerent escas, et malum inopiae temperarent.",
            "english": "And all provinces came into Egypt, to buy food, and to seek some relief of their want."
            "latin": "Emptusque est ager, et antrum quod in eo est, a filiis Heth.",
            "english": "'The field and the cave within it were purchased from the sons of Heth.'"
          },
          {
            "number": 33,
            "latin": "Mortuusque est Ioseph centum decem annorum: et embalzamaverunt eum, et conditus est in loculo in Aegypto.",
            "english": "After Joseph died at one hundred and ten years old, he was embalmed and placed in a sarcophagus in Egypt."
